# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# accounts.tsv — the single source of truth for WHICH ACCOUNT governs each repo.
#
# Read by:  bin/check-accounts (verifies)  ·  bin/connect-account (answers from it)
#           hooks/gate-accounts.py (blocks a push to a repo declared elsewhere)
#
# 📦 THIS FILE IS INSTANCE DATA. It describes YOUR accounts and YOUR repos.
#    A clone receives it with this header and ZERO rows — nobody inherits
#    somebody else's accounts. It is gitignored for the same reason.
#
# ⛔ NEVER PUT A TOKEN, A PASSWORD OR A KEY HERE. Not even temporarily.
#    The `guia` column points at a file under secrets/, which is outside git.
#    This file says WHERE credentials live; it never says WHAT they are.
#
# ⭐ WHY IT EXISTS, and it is not bookkeeping:
#    When several accounts are in play, "which one governs this repo" is a fact
#    that lives in three places at once — the remote, the docs, and someone's
#    memory — and nothing compares them. They drift, and the drift is silent:
#    work gets pushed to the wrong account, or to a repo that was retired
#    months ago, and the push succeeds. A declaration that no script checks is
#    a claim; this file exists so a script can check it against the machine.
#
# ⚠️ THE TRAP TO KNOW ABOUT: a renamed or transferred repository usually keeps
#    redirecting from its old address. Both names resolve, both look alive, and
#    a stale row can point at a dead repo and still appear to work. Re-measure
#    with `git remote -v`; never trust the row alone.
#
# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#
# FORMAT — TAB-separated, one row per repository:
#
#   repo   cuenta   rol   remoto   ruta_local   por_que_existe   guia
#
#   repo             owner/name as the host spells it
#   cuenta           which account governs it — the identity that may push
#   rol              what it is FOR (see the roles below)
#   remoto           the git remote name it answers to (origin, backup, …)
#                    or `-` when there is no local clone
#   ruta_local       where it lives on this machine, or `-` if not cloned
#                    ⚠️ a repo with no local path has never been verified
#                       against the machine — the row is a claim, not a fact
#   por_que_existe   ⭐ MANDATORY. One line. A repo that cannot justify itself
#                    is either duplicated work or abandoned work
#   guia             a file under secrets/ with the access steps, or `-`
#                    ⛔ the pointer, never the credential
#
# ── THE ROLES ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#   taller       the working repo — where daily work is pushed
#   backup       a verified copy of the product; not the working surface
#   motor        the engine itself, when you maintain one
#   control      tooling or orchestration around the work
#   sitio        a public site — ⚠️ pushing may publish
#   publicado    released for third parties, usually under a public licence
#   plantilla    a template others start from
#   archivado    ⛔ RETIRED — receives no work. Kept declared on purpose:
#                a repo that disappears from this table becomes invisible
#                again, and the reason it was retired disappears with it
#
# ⭐ Add your own roles if you need them, but declare each one here first.
#    A role used and not declared is a role the validator cannot check, and
#    it will pass silently — which is how a retired repo keeps receiving work.
#
# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
repo	cuenta	rol	remoto	ruta_local	por_que_existe	guia
#
# ⬜ YOUR ROWS GO BELOW. The file ships with none.
#
# Example of the shape — ⚠️ THIS IS A COMMENT, NOT A ROW. Copy it, remove the
# leading "#", and replace every value. Columns are separated by a TAB, never
# by spaces:
#
# my-org/my-app	my-account	taller	origin	~/my-app	where the product is built day to day	-
